# Corresponding Tests Required

**100% coverage of the change delta:** when adding or significantly changing a **function**
(or equivalent: method, exported helper, CLI subcommand handler), also add or update a
**corresponding test** in the same change. Do not leave new/changed functions untested.
Follow skill `.cursor/skills/require-corresponding-tests`.

## Applies to

| Language / area | Put production code in | Put tests in |
|---|---|---|
| Python (`monitoring/`) | `monitoring/data-collector/`, `monitoring/scripts/` | `monitoring/tests/test_*.py` (`unittest`) |
| Dashboard JS helpers | `monitoring/data-collector/static/dashboard-lib.js` | `monitoring/tests/test_dashboard_lib.js` (`node --test`) |
| Dashboard UI wiring | `monitoring/data-collector/static/app.js` | Prefer extracting pure logic into `dashboard-lib.js` + test there |
| Bash (`vstorm`, helpers, workload scripts) | `vstorm`, `helpers/`, `workload/`, `tests/helpers.bash` | `tests/*.bats` |

## Rules

1. **New function → new test** covering happy path and at least one edge/error case when non-trivial.
2. **Changed behavior → update the matching test** so expectations stay truthful (do not weaken tests only to go green — see `test-fix-discipline.mdc`).
3. **Pure logic over untested DOM/CLI glue**: prefer putting logic in testable helpers (`dashboard-lib.js`, Python modules) rather than only in UI event handlers or large bash scripts.
4. **Same PR / commit**: ship the test with the implementation, not as a follow-up.
5. **Run the suite** for the language you touched before finishing (see `pre-commit-checks.mdc`).

## Exceptions (document in the PR/commit body if used)

- Trivial one-line wrappers that only forward to an already-tested function
- Generated code or pure config with no behavior
- Prototype spikes explicitly marked temporary (must add tests before merge)
